HARNESS CONTRACT (the gates verify every point below mechanically):

You write ONLY `src/lib.rs`. A fixed, pre-generated `src/main.rs` CLI
shell (and separate fuzz targets) call into it, so lib.rs MUST export
exactly this interface:

  /// (op_name, runner) registry — one entry per operation.
  pub fn ops() -> Vec<(&'static str, fn(&[u8], u64) -> String)>

  /// Write, for EVERY operation with "needs_input": true, exactly two
  /// DISTINCT, VALID input files: <dir>/<op>.1.bin and <dir>/<op>.2.bin
  /// (deterministic bytes — same files on every run). You may call the
  /// library itself to synthesize them (e.g. use the encoder to produce
  /// inputs for a decode operation). Return one line per file:
  /// `seed <op> <path>`.
  pub fn gen_seeds(dir: &str) -> Vec<String>

  /// Write, for each operation whose work SCALES with input size, ONE input
  /// `<dir>/<op>.perf.bin` that is LARGE and REALISTIC enough that the
  /// operation's inner loop — not per-call setup/malloc/memset/libc —
  /// dominates a profiled run (the library's own code should account for the
  /// bulk of the time). This usually needs SEVERAL MEGABYTES, not a few KB.
  ///
  /// The data MUST be REALISTIC for the operation, NOT random/uniform bytes.
  /// Random or degenerate data makes many kernels take a trivial path and stay
  /// cold: compressors/matchers find no repeats, parsers/decoders hit an early
  /// error and bail, searches find nothing. Generate data with the STRUCTURE
  /// and REDUNDANCY that real inputs of this domain have (repeated substrings,
  /// valid records/tokens, realistic value distributions) so the hot loop runs
  /// to completion over the whole input.
  ///
  /// The input MUST be a VALID input the operation processes end-to-end — one
  /// that is accepted, not rejected at a format/length/validation gate (a
  /// rejected input measures error handling, not the kernel). For an operation
  /// whose input is an ENCODED/COMPRESSED/PACKED blob (decode/decompress/
  /// verify/inverse), PRODUCE that blob by first running the FORWARD direction
  /// (the library's own encoder/compressor) over a large realistic buffer,
  /// then feed the result — do NOT hand a decoder raw or random bytes.
  ///
  /// Rules of thumb by category: text/format parsers → a large valid document
  /// with many records; codecs/compressors → a big buffer of realistic,
  /// compressible content; hashers → a big realistic data block; decoders →
  /// the encoder's output over such content; matrix/DP/search kernels → large
  /// dimensions / a long realistic haystack. Deterministic bytes. Operations
  /// whose work does NOT scale with input (config/option/getter/free ops)
  /// SHOULD be omitted — functional-only, not perf targets. Return one line
  /// per file written: `perf <op> <path>`.
  pub fn gen_perf(dir: &str) -> Vec<String>

Each runner fn takes (input_bytes, iters) and RETURNS the digest line(s)
as a String (no trailing newline needed; the shell prints it).

Hard rules:
  1. DETERMINISM: identical (input, iters) → identical returned String.
     Never include pointers/addresses, time, PIDs, paths, or HashMap
     iteration order. Floating-point values must be folded into an
     integer checksum (e.g. to_bits()), never formatted as decimals.
     CRITICAL — a raw pointer VALUE is an address even when masked:
     NEVER `fold(digest, some_ptr as u64)` or `as usize & 0xFF`. A
     function returning a `*mut`/`*const` (e.g. lodepng_chunk_next) gives
     an address — fold a CONTENT-derived fact instead: whether it is null
     (`p.is_null() as u64`), or its OFFSET from a known base
     (`(p as usize).wrapping_sub(base as usize) as u64`). An address low
     byte looks stable within one build but changes across builds/hosts,
     silently rotting the golden oracle.
  2. INPUT-SENSITIVITY: the digest MUST depend on the input bytes
     (<op>.1.bin and <op>.2.bin must yield different digests).
  3. ERRORS ARE DATA — NEVER EXIT OR PANIC: these runners are also used
     as fuzz targets fed with arbitrary malformed bytes. When the
     library reports an error, fold the error code into the digest
     (e.g. return "op=decode err=83 digest=0") and return normally.
     No std::process::exit, no panics/unwrap on input-dependent values,
     no slice indexing that can go out of bounds on short inputs.
  4. ITERS: when iters > 1, re-run the operation each iteration and fold
     each iteration's digest into a running wrapping checksum; return
     the digest once at the end. Iterations must not accumulate state
     that changes results (re-init library state each iteration).
  5. The heavy lifting must happen INSIDE the library-under-test; the
     harness only feeds inputs and folds outputs (checksum over output
     buffers, counts, sizes). Do not re-implement library logic.
  6. Free / clean up library-allocated buffers with the library's own
     free functions where provided (also on error paths — no leaks per
     iteration, fuzzing runs millions of executions).
  7. Runner fns registered in ops() must be safe `fn` items (wrap the
     unsafe FFI work inside the function body).
  8. PER-MODULE DUPLICATE TYPES (c2rust gotcha): c2rust emits the SAME C
     struct as a DISTINCT Rust type in EVERY module that references it —
     e.g. `json_tokener::json_object`, `json_patch::json_object` and
     `json_object::json_object` are three different types with IDENTICAL
     layout. The compiler will NOT unify them: passing a pointer returned by
     one module's fn into another module's fn is an E0308 `mismatched types`
     (`expected *mut a::T, found *mut b::T`). To bridge, CAST THE RAW POINTER
     at the call boundary: `foo_from_mod_b(p as *mut _)` (or
     `p as *const _` / `p.cast()`). Pick ONE module's type as canonical per
     struct and cast every cross-module pointer to it. Never assume two
     same-named structs from different modules are the same type, and never
     transmute whole values — cast the pointer.


EXAMPLE SHAPE (for a DIFFERENT crate, libcsv — shows the expected style;
note MaybeUninit::zeroed for C structs, safe runner wrapping unsafe FFI,
error-as-data, checksum fold):

```rust
use std::fs;
use std::mem::MaybeUninit;
use libcsv_raw::src::libcsv::{csv_parser, csv_init, csv_parse, csv_fini, csv_free};

fn fold(acc: u64, x: u64) -> u64 { acc.rotate_left(1) ^ x }

pub fn op_parse(data: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_err = 0i32;
    for _ in 0..iters {
        unsafe {
            let mut st = MaybeUninit::<csv_parser>::zeroed();
            let p = st.as_mut_ptr();
            csv_init(p, 0);
            // … feed `data` through csv_parse with counting callbacks;
            //   on parse error, record it and keep going (error is data) …
            last_err = 0; // e.g. csv_error(p)
            csv_fini(p, None, None, std::ptr::null_mut());
            csv_free(p);
        }
        digest = fold(digest, /* rows */ 0).wrapping_add(/* fields */ 0);
    }
    format!("op=parse err={} digest={:016x}", last_err, digest)
}

pub fn ops() -> Vec<(&'static str, fn(&[u8], u64) -> String)> {
    vec![("parse", op_parse as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String)]
}

pub fn gen_seeds(dir: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    let mut lines = Vec::new();
    let s1 = b"a,b,c\n1,2,3\n".to_vec();          // deterministic bytes
    let s2 = b"x;y\n\"q,uo\",z\n7,8,9\n".to_vec();
    for (op, idx, bytes) in [("parse", 1, &s1), ("parse", 2, &s2)] {
        let path = format!("{}/{}.{}.bin", dir, op, idx);
        fs::write(&path, bytes).unwrap();
        lines.push(format!("seed {} {}", op, path));
    }
    lines
}

pub fn gen_perf(dir: &str) -> Vec<String> {
    // one LARGE realistic input per perf-relevant op (here: a big CSV so
    // csv_parse's scanning loop dominates, not per-call setup)
    let mut big = Vec::new();
    for i in 0..200_000u32 { big.extend_from_slice(format!("f{},{},{}\n", i, i*7, i^0x55).as_bytes()); }
    let path = format!("{}/parse.perf.bin", dir);
    fs::write(&path, &big).unwrap();
    vec![format!("perf parse {}", path)]
}
```


Notes for THIS crate:
- Every library call is `unsafe extern "C"`: use raw pointers,
  MaybeUninit::<T>::zeroed() for C structs, and the library's own
  init/cleanup functions.
- The dependency is already declared in Cargo.toml; just `use` it.
- Do NOT add external crates (std only).

Output the single complete file in one ```rust block.

----- OUTPUT -----
```rust
use std::ffi::CStr;
use std::fs;
use std::mem::MaybeUninit;
use std::os::raw::{c_char, c_int, c_long, c_void};
use std::ptr;

use fzy_raw::src::choices::{
    choices_add, choices_available, choices_destroy, choices_fread, choices_get, choices_getscore,
    choices_init, choices_next, choices_prev, choices_search, choices_t,
};
use fzy_raw::src::options::{options_init, options_t};
use fzy_raw::src::r#match::{has_match, match_0, match_positions, strcasechr};

extern "C" {
    fn tmpfile() -> *mut c_void;
    fn fwrite(ptr: *const c_void, size: usize, nmemb: usize, stream: *mut c_void) -> usize;
    fn rewind(stream: *mut c_void);
    fn fclose(stream: *mut c_void) -> c_int;
}

fn fold(acc: u64, x: u64) -> u64 {
    acc.rotate_left(5) ^ x.wrapping_mul(0x9E37_79B1_85EB_CA87)
}

fn fold_bytes(mut acc: u64, bytes: &[u8]) -> u64 {
    for &b in bytes {
        acc = fold(acc, b as u64);
    }
    acc
}

fn fold_usize(acc: u64, x: usize) -> u64 {
    fold(acc, x as u64)
}

fn fold_mem<T>(acc: u64, v: &T) -> u64 {
    let p = v as *const T as *const u8;
    let n = std::mem::size_of::<T>();
    if n == 0 {
        return fold(acc, 0);
    }
    let bytes = unsafe { std::slice::from_raw_parts(p, n) };
    fold_bytes(acc, bytes)
}

fn sanitize_c_bytes(input: &[u8]) -> Vec<u8> {
    let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(input.len() + 1);
    for &b in input {
        out.push(if b == 0 { b' ' } else { b });
    }
    out.push(0);
    out
}

fn split_once_nul(data: &[u8]) -> (&[u8], &[u8]) {
    if let Some(i) = data.iter().position(|&b| b == 0) {
        (&data[..i], &data[i + 1..])
    } else {
        (data, &[])
    }
}

fn split_query_and_rest(data: &[u8]) -> (&[u8], &[u8]) {
    if let Some(i) = data.iter().position(|&b| b == b'\n') {
        (&data[..i], &data[i + 1..])
    } else {
        (data, &[])
    }
}

fn checksum_cstr_ptr(mut acc: u64, s: *const c_char) -> u64 {
    if s.is_null() {
        return fold(acc, 0);
    }
    unsafe {
        let bytes = CStr::from_ptr(s).to_bytes();
        acc = fold_bytes(acc, bytes);
        fold(acc, bytes.len() as u64)
    }
}

fn build_line_cstrings(data: &[u8]) -> (Vec<u8>, Vec<Vec<u8>>) {
    let mut parts = data.split(|&b| b == b'\n');
    let query = sanitize_c_bytes(parts.next().unwrap_or(&[]));
    let mut lines = Vec::new();
    for part in parts {
        if !part.is_empty() {
            lines.push(sanitize_c_bytes(part));
        }
    }
    (query, lines)
}

unsafe fn with_temp_file_bytes(bytes: &[u8]) -> Result<*mut c_void, i32> {
    let f = tmpfile();
    if f.is_null() {
        return Err(1);
    }
    if !bytes.is_empty() {
        let wrote = fwrite(bytes.as_ptr() as *const c_void, 1, bytes.len(), f);
        if wrote != bytes.len() {
            fclose(f);
            return Err(2);
        }
    }
    rewind(f);
    Ok(f)
}

pub fn op_match_primitives(data: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_err = 0i32;

    for _ in 0..iters {
        let (needle_raw, hay_raw) = split_once_nul(data);
        let needle = sanitize_c_bytes(needle_raw);
        let haystack = sanitize_c_bytes(hay_raw);

        let mut iter_digest = 0u64;
        unsafe {
            let needle_ptr = needle.as_ptr() as *const c_char;
            let hay_ptr = haystack.as_ptr() as *const c_char;

            let first_ch = needle_raw.first().copied().unwrap_or(0) as c_char;
            let p = strcasechr(hay_ptr, first_ch);
            let offset = if p.is_null() {
                usize::MAX
            } else {
                (p as usize).wrapping_sub(hay_ptr as usize)
            };
            iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, offset);

            let hm = has_match(needle_ptr, hay_ptr);
            iter_digest = fold(iter_digest, hm as u64);

            let s1 = match_0(needle_ptr, hay_ptr);
            iter_digest = fold_mem(iter_digest, &s1);

            let pos_len = needle_raw.len();
            let mut positions = vec![usize::MAX; pos_len];
            let pos_ptr = if positions.is_empty() {
                ptr::null_mut()
            } else {
                positions.as_mut_ptr()
            };
            let s2 = match_positions(needle_ptr, hay_ptr, pos_ptr);
            iter_digest = fold_mem(iter_digest, &s2);

            for &pos in &positions {
                iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, pos);
            }
            iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, needle_raw.len());
            iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, hay_raw.len());
            last_err = 0;
        }

        digest = fold(digest, iter_digest);
    }

    format!("op=match_primitives err={} digest={:016x}", last_err, digest)
}

pub fn op_choices_add_search(data: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_err = 0i32;

    for _ in 0..iters {
        let (query, lines) = build_line_cstrings(data);
        let mut iter_digest = 0u64;

        unsafe {
            let mut opt = MaybeUninit::<options_t>::zeroed();
            options_init(opt.as_mut_ptr());

            let mut ch = MaybeUninit::<choices_t>::zeroed();
            let chp = ch.as_mut_ptr();
            choices_init(chp, opt.as_mut_ptr() as *mut _);

            for line in &lines {
                choices_add(chp, line.as_ptr() as *const c_char);
            }

            choices_search(chp, query.as_ptr() as *const c_char);

            let avail = choices_available(chp);
            iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, avail);

            let limit = std::cmp::min(avail as usize, 5);
            for i in 0..limit {
                let s = choices_get(chp, i);
                iter_digest = checksum_cstr_ptr(iter_digest, s);
                let sc = choices_getscore(chp, i);
                iter_digest = fold_mem(iter_digest, &sc);
            }

            let before = choices_get(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = checksum_cstr_ptr(iter_digest, before);
            let before_sc = choices_getscore(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = fold_mem(iter_digest, &before_sc);

            choices_prev(chp);
            let after_prev = choices_get(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = checksum_cstr_ptr(iter_digest, after_prev);
            let after_prev_sc = choices_getscore(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = fold_mem(iter_digest, &after_prev_sc);

            choices_next(chp);
            let after_next = choices_get(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = checksum_cstr_ptr(iter_digest, after_next);
            let after_next_sc = choices_getscore(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = fold_mem(iter_digest, &after_next_sc);

            iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, lines.len());
            iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, query.len().saturating_sub(1));

            choices_destroy(chp);
            last_err = 0;
        }

        digest = fold(digest, iter_digest);
    }

    format!("op=choices_add_search err={} digest={:016x}", last_err, digest)
}

pub fn op_choices_fread_search(data: &[u8], iters: u64) -> String {
    let mut digest = 0u64;
    let mut last_err = 0i32;

    for _ in 0..iters {
        let (query_raw, payload) = split_query_and_rest(data);
        let query = sanitize_c_bytes(query_raw);
        let mut iter_digest = 0u64;

        unsafe {
            let mut opt = MaybeUninit::<options_t>::zeroed();
            options_init(opt.as_mut_ptr());

            let mut ch = MaybeUninit::<choices_t>::zeroed();
            let chp = ch.as_mut_ptr();
            choices_init(chp, opt.as_mut_ptr() as *mut _);

            match with_temp_file_bytes(payload) {
                Ok(f) => {
                    choices_fread(chp, f as *mut _, b'\n' as c_char);
                    let _ = fclose(f);
                    last_err = 0;
                }
                Err(code) => {
                    last_err = code;
                }
            }

            choices_search(chp, query.as_ptr() as *const c_char);

            let avail = choices_available(chp);
            iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, avail);

            let limit = std::cmp::min(avail as usize, 5);
            for i in 0..limit {
                let s = choices_get(chp, i);
                iter_digest = checksum_cstr_ptr(iter_digest, s);
                let sc = choices_getscore(chp, i);
                iter_digest = fold_mem(iter_digest, &sc);
            }

            choices_prev(chp);
            let p0 = choices_get(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = checksum_cstr_ptr(iter_digest, p0);
            let p0s = choices_getscore(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = fold_mem(iter_digest, &p0s);

            choices_next(chp);
            let n0 = choices_get(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = checksum_cstr_ptr(iter_digest, n0);
            let n0s = choices_getscore(chp, 0);
            iter_digest = fold_mem(iter_digest, &n0s);

            iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, payload.len());
            iter_digest = fold_usize(iter_digest, query_raw.len());

            choices_destroy(chp);
        }

        digest = fold(digest, iter_digest ^ (last_err as u64));
    }

    format!(
        "op=choices_fread_search err={} digest={:016x}",
        last_err, digest
    )
}

pub fn ops() -> Vec<(&'static str, fn(&[u8], u64) -> String)> {
    vec![
        ("match_primitives", op_match_primitives as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String),
        (
            "choices_add_search",
            op_choices_add_search as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String,
        ),
        (
            "choices_fread_search",
            op_choices_fread_search as fn(&[u8], u64) -> String,
        ),
    ]
}

